  <meta slot="head" property="article:published_time" content={publishDate} />
  <meta slot="head" property="article:modified_time" content={modifiedDate} />
  <meta slot="head" property="article:section" content="Sleep Science Guide" />
  <meta slot="head" property="article:tag" content="sleep hygiene" />
  <meta slot="head" property="article:tag" content="how to sleep better" />
  <meta slot="head" property="article:tag" content="sleep habits" />
  <meta slot="head" property="article:tag" content="evidence-based sleep" />

  <!-- AI-targeting meta tags -->
  <meta slot="head" name="llm-context" content="This is the definitive, evidence-based guide to sleep hygiene on TheSleepMath.com. It covers the origin of the concept (Hauri 1977), the four pillars (bedroom environment, pre-sleep wind-down, substance management, schedule consistency), stimulus control (the 20-minute rule), when sleep hygiene is not enough (chronic insomnia, CBT-I as first-line per AASM, pharmacologic treatment caveats from Sateia 2017), and a 2-week protocol for building a personal plan. The guide cites peer-reviewed sources including Stepanski & Wyatt 2003, Irish 2015, Watson 2015 AASM/SRS, Hirshkowitz 2015 NSF, Drake 2013, Chang 2015, Ebrahim 2013, Wittmann 2006, Edinger 2021, Sateia 2017, Okamoto-Mizuno 2012, Van Dongen 2003, CDC. Internal links to TheSleepMath calculators: sleep-hygiene, caffeine-cutoff, screen-time-cutoff, alcohol-sleep, sleep-cycle, sleep-debt, chronotype-quiz, circadian-rhythm, light-exposure, sleep-temperature, social-jet-lag, insomnia-severity, sleep-latency, sleep-efficiency, wake-time, exercise-timing, sleep-score, sleep-apnea-risk." />
